Now to talk about a mod that came out in mid-February, a mod known professionally as Funkin’ Remnants
For those of you curious, yes, this is the same Remnants as the Funkin’ Remnants Twitter account 
(one of my all time favorite Funkin’ accounts ever)
The wireframe designs and funky beats make this mod one of my favorite since Spaghetti dropped 
(which makes it sound like I play mods all the time, but I don’t, this is the only one I’ve played since the SP Collab)
If you’re not a fan of aesthetics and chromatics, then not to worry, you can definitely practice your FNF skills too

Some of the songs are more difficult than the original FNF ratings (with the highest being 15 stars for Remnants Pico Blazin’)
I will definitely continue to be playing this mod to practice whenever I feel like it
This mod is actually GREAT practice for the main game, as most of the levels follow the same structure as the more modern Weekend 1 and SP Collab
, where the notes are a bit more spaced out and not cluttered unlike Cocoa and Eggnog
However, there are levels that, when played on Hard mode, will give you a run for your money, 
like the aforementioned Blazin’ level and also Thorns Remnants Mix
